Z||000000||Justice||06-25-2001||06:00 PM||||Hello All<BR> I just bought a 84 about a month ago how hard would it be to put a 2.8 in a 84 sport coupe if i could find a cradle,tranny and motor all together from a junk yard and what would be the best year to get the 2.8 out of<P>P.S.<BR>Thanks for any help ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||06-25-2001||06:09 PM||||I also have an 84 sc, but still with the oem motor. From what I can tell.... 84's were the only years the did not offer a 2.8, and they were wired a bit different. So that may make it a bit more difficult compared to like an 85, but still doable, just get as may wires as you can from the donor car.<P>Dont let them cut the wires and also make sure you get the ecm too. too answer your question I would think any 85-87 car would be easiest. I dont know about an 88 though, but if it would work then you may handle a bit better.||||reg||1
